From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Juan Pablo Lassala <jpablolassala@gmail.com>
Date: Sat, 24 Oct 2026 12:00:00 -0300
Subject: [PATCH] toplevel: Float a panel off its edge under Caminito

A panel could only be lined up with its screen edge, which Plasma's floating
panel isn't.

A panel has a Floating property, a key of its schema, in its properties
below Autohide. Under Caminito, the Wayland compositor, a floating panel
stands off the edge it is at by a gap of 8 pixels, which is the layer-shell
margin of that edge, and its corners are rounded, with no frame. The
exclusive zone is the panel's size as before: the compositor counts the
margin in it, so a maximized window ends where the panel does, not behind
it. A panel that isn't expanded keeps being centred along its edge, since it
is anchored to the edge alone, and an expanded one reaches both of its
sides. An autohidden panel leaves its strip at the edge, and a drawer opens
from where its floating panel is.

Without an owner of org.mate.Caminito, which is X11 and any other Wayland
compositor, and for a drawer, the key does nothing and the properties have
no row for it.
